{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/708804-source-material-vs-null-mysteriis","id":708804,"title":"Source material vs. Null Mysteriis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-19T09:16:53-07:00","id":708804,"title":"Source material vs. Null Mysteriis","content":"Most of the mentions of the Null Mysteriis in the base book and the few splats I own kinda make them out to be dolts who are in over their heads in most situations. That depiction doesn't sit particularly well with me, as I find myself liking the idea of some dyed-in-the-wool scientist/hunters who watch a Cthulhu beast rise from the sea and heft a camera in one hand and a high-powered rifle in the other. But the source material seems very ready to write them off as 'yeah, they're in the setting, whatevs, let's glurge about the Cheiron Group some more.' <br /> <br /> There's been rising interest in a Changeling game in my area, and I was thinking of having some hunters as prominent antagonists running up the ambient fear of the setting. I was originally pretty solidly for the Aegis Kai Doru as the villains, specifically as a sort of bull-in-a-china-shop force that knows just enough about the True Fae and not enough about changelings to think that changeling equals privateer, and the different courts are different cult-style recruitment methods for setting up kidnapping victims.<br /> <br /> But after reviewing my Hunter books again, I'm kinda itching to make the Null Mysteriis badass, and most importantly to the story I want to tell, have them be a convertible bad guy -- and by that I mean, if the PCs direct labor towards it, they can turn the hunters onto the True Fae only, and be left in peace. Null Mysteriis seems like they might be amenable to such an idea -- once some psychologists get unrestricted access to Court society, they're likely to discover that changelings are a society of abuse victims with different methods of coping, rather than an invasion beachhead.<br /> <br /> I've got some ideas for how I'd do this, but I'm curious, is there more Null Mysteriis stuff in the other hunter books? I'm busting for other ideas to get my juices flowing. If you have any ideas of your own, feel free to post them here, too. I don't mind, I'm looking for help whatever the source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T09:27:30-07:00","id":708858,"title":"","content":"As one of the original six compacts, every hunter book released has something on them. Of course, some handle it better than others, but so long as their theme of putting science to the supernatural is intact, you should be good. Though I feel like you're basically going to doom entire cells by putting them onto the path of the true fae.<br /> <br /> If you accept fan material, Kings Raven and I made a fan book directly dealing with how hunters and changelings interact with an entire section on Null Mysteriis and changeling interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T17:28:16-07:00","id":709587,"title":"","content":"I support the idea of a more kick-ass Null Mysteriis. Admittedly, they do seem to be merely curious researchers (and not particularly well funded researchers, at that). The core book and the Compacts &amp; Conspiracies pdf both hint at a faction, the Cataclysmicists, lead by a woman named Khalili (spelling?) She is a candidate for an upcoming General Secretary election within the NM. In my setting, she's motivated to tear the veil between worlds, because how else can scientists effectively examine the unknown?<br /> <br /> The NM could be terrifying if they have access to big science stuff: Large Hadron Collider, atomic weaponry, or mother f---king lasers. I mean, it could get pretty ridiculous, but it's just a thought. Also, I agree that the True Fae would distract attention away from changelings. Why mess with changelings when you can study the origin of these creatures? When it's publish or perish in some academic communities, a member could be highly motivated to get a True Fae brain in this jar, right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Improper use of inverted commas, Hoover!&quot; - Herr Starr","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8536-nutshell","name":"Nutshell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T03:06:59-07:00","id":710276,"title":"","content":"I don't think True Fae <i>have </i>brains that can be put in a jar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T03:28:50-07:00","id":710292,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer Null Mysteriis being about science and discovery rather than kicking ass, but it's your game so I'll just point out how very very observable Wyrd, Fate, and faerie magic can be.<br /> <br /> What are the odds of a girl who grew up as a virtual slave to her stepmother and two older stepsisters marrying an attractive celebrity? How often does it actually happen in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> For good scientists with computers and statistics it's not hard to realise that popular faerie tales are way more common than they should be, and once you start figuring out how fate works you can do awesome science to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T06:11:02-07:00","id":710446,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the contractional nature of Fae Magic seems like a serious boon to rigorous empirical testing, even if they follow their own logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T07:25:18-07:00","id":710522,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Question as one of its senior members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T17:27:58-07:00","id":711471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/708804-source-material-vs-null-mysteriis?p=710276#post710276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think True Fae <i>have </i>brains that can be put in a jar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're right, but some unlucky Null Mysteriis member should verify that. Just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Improper use of inverted commas, Hoover!&quot; - Herr Starr","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8536-nutshell","name":"Nutshell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T17:37:40-07:00","id":711482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/708804-source-material-vs-null-mysteriis?p=710276#post710276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think True Fae <i>have </i>brains that can be put in a jar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a small few don't, I reckon. THeir plots often demand some kind of biological processor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T17:52:47-07:00","id":711496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For good scientists with computers and statistics it's not hard to realise that popular faerie tales are way more common than they should be, and once you start figuring out how fate works you can do awesome science to it. </div> </div> </div>Or the simpler rationale that fairy tales reflect actual reality which people assume is less likely than in fact it is. You can only really estimate the probability of something like a fairytale coming true by frequency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T18:05:30-07:00","id":711516,"title":"","content":"Yes, I like them more as voyeur hunters like Network Zero. There to find out, to gather proof, not exactly to commit genocide. If Null Mysteriis becomes more about killing shit, aren't they then just the Union with college degrees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}